// Welcome to PoeziCode!
// Write on the left; "Compile" (F5) creates the PDF on the right.
// All commands are listed under "Docs" – or type @ for suggestions.

@document[paper=A4, margin=2.5cm, font=serif, fontsize=11, lang=en]
@header{PoeziCode}{}{@today}
@footer{}{Page @page of @pages}{}

// Custom commands: #1, #2 … are the arguments.
@define{poezi}{@color[turquoise]{@bold{PoeziCode}}}
@define{stress}{@bold{@color[magenta]{#1}}}

@title{Welcome to PoeziCode}
@subtitle{Write documents like code}
@author{PoeziCode}
@date

@toc

@pagebreak

@chapter{First steps}

A paragraph is simply text. An @bold{empty line} starts a new paragraph.
Single line breaks in the source become spaces – just like in LaTeX.

Inside a paragraph you can write @italic{italic}, @underline{underlined},
@strike{struck through}, @highlight{highlighted} or @code{code} – and of
course @color[red]{coloured} text. This is @poezi, a custom command, and this
is @stress{with an argument}. Water is H@sub{2}O, an area measures 3 m@sup{2}.

@note{
  Every command starts with @code{@}. Arguments go into @code{\{ \}}, options
  into @code{[ ]}. Write an @-sign itself as @code{\@} and a comment with
  @code{//}. With @code{@newln} at the end this box gets one line taller. @newln
}

@section{Alignment}

@left{This sentence is on the left.}
@center{This sentence is centred.}
@right{And this one is on the right.}

@align[justify]{With @code{@align[justify]} a paragraph is justified – flush with
both margins as soon as it is long enough to run over several lines. The same works
with @code{@align[left]}, @code{@align[center]} and @code{@align[right]}.}

@section{Spacing}

With @code{@block[…]{…}} any block gets spacing like a @code{<div>} in HTML:
@code{top} and @code{bottom} push it down or pull it closer with negative values,
@code{left} and @code{right} indent it, and @code{shift} moves only the block itself.
Lengths also work in lines, e.g. @code{top=2ln}.

@block[top=1ln, left=1.5cm, right=1.5cm]{
  @note[Indented]{This box sits one line lower and is indented by 1.5 cm on both sides.}
}

@section{Lists}

@list{
  @item{Bulleted lists with @code{@list}}
  @item{Numbered lists with @code{@numbered}:
    @numbered{
      @item{lists can be nested,}
      @item{as deep as you like.}
    }
  }
  @item{Links like @link{https://github.com}{this one} are clickable.}
}

@section{Tables}

@table[header]{
  @row{Command | Effect | Example}
  @row{@code{@bold} | bold | @bold{Text}}
  @row{@code{@italic} | italic | @italic{Text}}
  @row{@code{$…$} | inline formula | $x^2 + y^2 = r^2$}
}

@chapter{Math}

Inline formulas go between dollar signs: $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$ or
$e^{i@pi} + 1 = 0$. Displayed formulas go between double dollar signs.
The quadratic formula:

$$ x_{1,2} = @frac{-b +- @sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} $$

Sums, integrals and limits get their bounds with @code{_} and @code{^}:

$$ @sum_{k=1}^{n} k^2 = @frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6} $$

$$ @integral_{-@infty}^{@infty} e^{-x^2} dx = @sqrt{@pi} $$

$$ lim_{n -> @infty} @paren{1 + @frac{1}{n}}^n = e $$

Matrices, vectors and case distinctions:

$$ A = @matrix{ @row{1 & 2 & 3} @row{4 & 5 & 6} } ,  @vec{v} @in @R^3 $$

$$ @abs{x} = @cases{ @row{x & @text{if } x >= 0} @row{-x & @text{otherwise}} } $$

@section{Drawings and 3D}

@code{@drawing} creates sketches and function graphs right inside the document:

@drawing[axes, grid]{
  @plot{x^2 - 2}
  @plot[color=magenta, dashed]{2sin(x)}
  @point[below]{0,-2}{$S$}
  @label[right]{-3.8, 13}{$f(x) = x^2 - 2$}
}{Two functions in a coordinate system}

@surface{x^2 - y^2}{A saddle surface. Build your own 3D models in the CAD editor and insert them with @code{@model\{name\}}.}

@section{Code and quotes}

@codeblock[dart]{
  void main() {
    print('Hello from PoeziCode!');
  }
}

@quote{The limits of my language mean the limits of my world.}{Ludwig Wittgenstein}

@warning{Do not forget to save – with @bold{Ctrl+S}.}

@columns{
  @bold{Left:} With @code{@columns} content sits side by side.
}{
  @bold{Right:} Up to four columns are possible.
}

@rule

@center{Have fun writing! $@pi @approx 3.14159$}
